      { issue: "Duo won't power on", fix: "Power reaches a Duo through the hub: brick into the hub, hub cable into the base of the 14-inch display. Take the plate off the underside of the base with the green screwdriver and look at the connectors rather than assuming — the hub cable and the printer cable both terminate there and both are screwed down. Then unplug the display cord for 10 seconds, plug it back in and let it boot.", cat: "power" },
      { issue: "Tap or PIN doesn't work", fix: "On a Duo the card is read at the customer-facing terminal — Clover's own device documentation puts chip, tap and swipe there, and the 14-inch screen is for order entry. Test on the terminal, and get the tip jar, phone stand or propped-up menu off the front of it before you call the reader faulty.", cat: "card" },
      { issue: "Cash drawer never kicks", fix: "On a Duo the drawer hangs off the hub, not the printer. Clover's setup guide puts the small end of the drawer cable in the #2 jack on the hub, and there are two drawer-icon jacks there marked 1 and 2 — check which one it is actually in before you order a replacement drawer.", cat: "pinpad" },
      { issue: "Receipts stop but kitchen tickets keep printing", fix: "The Duo's own printer is cabled into the base of the display while kitchen printers sit on the LAN, so the two fail independently. Work the local side: Help app → menu → Diagnostics → Print Queue, clear it, fix the paper or the cable, then Retry Print Jobs. A pending job drops itself after 60 minutes and is gone.", cat: "receipt" },
      { issue: "Boot seems stuck at the Clover logo", fix: "The quick start guide has you hold the power button until the logo appears — after that, leave it alone. Boot takes 2–3 minutes; merchants pull the cord at 45 seconds and start the clock over.", cat: "power" },
      { issue: "Duo went offline after the counter was rearranged", fix: "Clover's setup guide runs the LAN into the network port on the hub, while the base of the display takes the three screw-down cables. Check both of those before you touch the router — on a Duo they are where a cable gets pulled loose without anyone noticing.", cat: "network" },
      { issue: "Nobody can tell which device rang an order", fix: "Give every device a prefix: Clover Merchant Dashboard → Setup → Devices → Order Title Prefix. Every order then carries the originating device in its title, which matters on a Duo site because staff share logins across the register and whatever else is on the counter.", cat: "reports" },
      { issue: "Which screen do we set it up on", fix: "Activation and order entry happen on the 14-inch merchant display; the customer terminal handles payment and signature. If a rep is being walked through setup over the phone, make sure they are looking at the merchant screen.", cat: "config" },
      { issue: "Merchant wants the Duo on cellular", fix: "V5.261 prices the Duo as an Ethernet / Wi-Fi bundle — full payout, no wireless fee line — unlike the Mini and Kiosk rows, which carry a $35 monthly wireless fee once 4G is activated. Do not quote a cellular Duo off this matrix; take it back to the office.", cat: "account" },
      { issue: "Cracked customer display — is it covered?", fix: "The Duo three-year care plan is $230 and covers accidental damage, cracked or broken screens, manufacturer defects and liquid damage, everywhere except New York. It does not cover theft, loss or fire. Check for an active plan before you quote a replacement.", cat: "account" },
      { issue: "Both screens are dead", fix: "The Station is powered through the receipt printer. Check the L-shaped cable is seated in the display at one end and the printer at the other, and that the power cable runs into the printer, not the display. If it has sat on power for 30 minutes with no Clover logo, escalate for a replacement.", cat: "power" },
      { issue: "Screens are lit but frozen", fix: "Hold the white power button on the bottom right side of the station for about 10 seconds. If it will not come back up, unplug the display cable from the bottom of the station, wait 10 seconds and reconnect it.", cat: "power" },
      { issue: "Customer display is blank", fix: "The 8-inch display connects by USB and runs on the USB Pay Display app. That app has to be installed and running on both units — the merchant screen and the customer screen. Check the customer unit first; that is the one that gets closed.", cat: "display" },
      { issue: "Customer screen frozen, merchant screen fine", fix: "Restart the whole system rather than the app. A frozen customer screen with a working merchant screen usually clears with a full system restart, and rarely clears by killing and reopening USB Pay Display.", cat: "display" },
      { issue: "Merchant plugged a laptop into the USB-C port", fix: "The Duo's USB-C port is proprietary and does not follow standard USB-C behaviour. Anything that is not Clover hardware can be damaged by it, so check the laptop or phone before you check the Duo. Treat that port as Clover-peripherals-only and say so out loud.", cat: "config" },
      { issue: "Duo shows Offline or Device is Disconnected", fix: "Go to Settings → Network → Ethernet (or Wi-Fi) → Forget network, then reconnect with the password. Forgetting and re-adding fixes far more than toggling the connection. If they are mid-rush, switch them into Offline Mode so they keep taking payments while you work it.", cat: "network" },
      { issue: "Everything went down at once", fix: "Check status.clover.com before you touch the station. A red or orange incident there means the problem is Clover's, and restarting a two-screen bundle during an incident wastes time and can make it worse. Put the merchant into Offline Mode and wait it out.", cat: "account" },
      { issue: "No cash drawer came with the bundle", fix: "Correct — the Duo bundle does not include one. The drawer is $150 to buy or $15 a month, connects by RJ11, and is driven by the receipt printer rather than by the station.", cat: "account" },
      { issue: "Can we swap something out of the bundle?", fix: "No. The Duo cannot be ordered out of bundle and there are no à-la-carte substitutions. If the pieces are wrong for this merchant, the answer is a different device, not a modified bundle.", cat: "compat" },
      { issue: "Kitchen tickets are firing from the wrong screen", fix: "Only one device can be the default firing device, set under Setup → Devices. On a Duo that is the station, not the customer display. If a new device was added and tickets still fire from the old one, the firing device was never switched — it will not move until the old device is fully deactivated.", cat: "firing" },
      { issue: "Online order is on the dashboard but not on the station", fix: "Check the payment status first. A declined card leaves the order visible in the web dashboard under Orders while the Orders app on the station never shows it. The Duo is behaving correctly and there is nothing to sync.", cat: "card" }
